Ingredient count is capacity, not evidence. The current build has 53 rows because each surviving row owns anatomy, plane, transition, pressure, diffusion, or a declared matrix function. The inventory-independent ideal has 57 rows because four current approximations are split into exact target materials; it is not “better” merely because it has four more lines.

## Spatial and temporal transition map

| Window | Front | Living middle | Rear / residue | Required relationship |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0–5 min | Bergamot, citron, aldehydic peel, wet Ginger EO | Linalyl body, citral flash, pale pepper | First violet-metal and cedar glints | Citrus exposes ginger; it must not become the subject |
| 5–45 min | Ginger surface contracts | Jessemal, dihydrojasmone, ethyl linalool, terpinyl acetate, and clary-stem seam reveal moist fiber | Leafovert/Dynascone/ionones and basil flower expand behind it | Ginger changes physical state instead of vanishing |
| 45 min–3 h | Violet-green fiber and dry pepper remain | Ionone cloth, muguet air, cedar/vetiver grain | Tonka-sandal yielding chamber and mineral contour | Shared woody/floral/fibrous edges make one handoff |
| 3–8 h+ | Dry cedar-vetiver outline | Coumarinic and sandalwood interior | Koavone/Ambrofix/Norlimbanol pressure with Romandolide aura | The base recalls ginger by dry fiber, warmth, and cut—not by retaining a literal top note |

All temporal language above is design intent, not observed evolution.

