## Missing-chemical impact gate

| Missing/depleted exact | Current approximation | Residual limitation | Impact | Recommendation |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Ginger CO2 Extract | Jessemal + Dihydrojasmone + Ethyl Linalool + diluted Clary Sage | Warm oily rhizome remains less literal than true CO2 | **High** for dual-state realism | Purchase P1 only after current topology survives blind identity/liking test |
| Violet Leaf Absolute 10% | Leafovert + Dynascone 10% + ionones + Scentenal 0.1% | Natural leafy-metallic complexity is synthetic and simplified | **High-medium** | Purchase P1 after violet arm survives |
| Cedarwood oil Virginia | Cedarwood EO + Himalayan Cedarwood + Timberol | Pencil-dry Virginia grain remains approximate | **Medium** | Restock P2 |
| Haitian Vetiver EO | Indian Vetiver + Vetikon + Vetival | Current root is darker/earthier and less clean-dry | **Medium** | Purchase P2 |
| White Pepper EO | Black Pepper EO at 20 uL | More earthy and less pale than ideal | **Medium-low** | Purchase P3 |
| Lemon FCF oil Sicilian | Cedrat FCF 20 uL + Lemonile 1% | More bitter-citron than literal lemon peel | **Medium-low** | Restock P3 |

No missing item blocks the theory build. The two high-impact materials block a claim of literal ginger/violet realism, not computational evaluation of the current architecture.

## Future mixing order — not executed

1. Prepare and verify every working stock first.
2. Combine quiet matrix, Romandolide, sandalwoods, pressure materials, cedar/vetiver materials, and allow complete integration.
3. Add ionone/violet cloth and floral-air materials.
4. Add ginger-interior materials, then Ginger EO and aromatic connectors.
5. Add citrus, pepper, aldehydes, Lemonile stock, and trace air materials last.
6. Bring concentrate to exactly 6,000 uL, then add 24,000 uL ethanol only in a separately authorized physical batch.

This sequence is a design protocol, not an observed solubility or maturation result.

## Controlled blinded topology test — future work

Question: do the added microfacets create connected identity-linked depth, or only more ingredients?

Protect the other 5,890 uL as a common identity core. Use one 80 uL fiber block and one non-overlapping 30 uL relief block, replacing each omitted block one-for-one with DPG:

- **FIBER+ (80 uL):** Jessemal increment 50 uL + Clary Sage EO 10% 10 uL + Beta Ionone 1% 20 uL. Tests warm rhizome body and aromatic recurrence into violet/vetiver.
- **RELIEF+ (30 uL):** Ebanol 10% 10 uL + Javanol 10% 10 uL + Scentenal 0.1% 10 uL. Tests front/rear micro-contrast and carved finishing.

| Arm | Common core | FIBER+ | RELIEF+ | DPG replacement | Total concentrate |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| A / 00 compressed control | 5890 | 0 | 0 | 110 | 6000 |
| B / 10 | 5890 | 80 | 0 | 30 | 6000 |
| C / 01 | 5890 | 0 | 30 | 80 | 6000 |
| D / 11 full V3 | 5890 | 80 | 30 | 0 | 6000 |

For any future physical test, prepare each full 6,000 uL concentrate master so all source aliquots meet the 10 uL floor, then take 600 uL concentrate + 2,400 uL ethanol for each coded 3 mL evaluation bottle. Prepare a second independent set from fresh masters for confirmation. Randomize anonymous codes; use balanced orders across assessors/sessions; keep the key sealed until ballots are locked.

Evaluate at 0, 5, 30, and 120 minutes, then 6 and 24 hours. Record free description first, then L'Homme recognizability, ginger surface, ginger interior, ginger-to-violet transition, violet-leaf realism, violet-to-wood transition, cedar/vetiver grain, airy/dense simultaneity, spatial depth, textural style, overall liking, muddiness, metallic glare, blue drift, iris drift, sweetness, fatigue, and whether the perfume reads as one object.

Identity loss rejects an arm before abstract depth. A stronger or more detailed arm is not automatically better. A null or discordant result is `HOLD/NON-INFORMATIVE` at this dose and protocol. The high-detail formula survives only if D preserves identity and improves at least one identity-linked depth/transition axis without worsening liking or drift.

## Final claim ceiling

This artifact is **theory plus computational experiment design only**. It is not physically compounded or smelled. No similarity, liking, luxury, complexity, depth, three-dimensionality, safety, stability, longevity, diffusion, maturation, or release claim is established.

